WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.960
Futurama is a cult hit now, but the first
time around, the second show from the creator

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.640
of The Simpsons was never given a real shot
to shine.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.680
Matt Groening became a true force in television
animation after creating The Simpsons, which

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.800
has aired an astonishing 600-plus episodes
on Fox since premiering 30 years ago in 1989.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.300
In the late 90's, with The Simpsons having
become a cultural phenomenon, Fox began to

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.680
express interest in a new show from Groening.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.960
He came back to Fox with the show that would
eventually become Futurama.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.680
"Shut up and take my money!"

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.560
It should have been a surefire hit.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.740
Instead, though, Groening says that Fox seemingly
never really wanted Futurama to succeed, and

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.900
even sabotaged their own show rather than
let Groening have another hit.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.180
During an interview with Mother Jones, Groening
had some not-so-great things to say about

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.200
working with Fox execs in Hollywood.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.860
"You can't believe what babies people are.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.540
It's really like being in junior high school."

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.200
Groening even said that Fox executives weren't
fans of The Simpsons either, revealing,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.360
"You can't expect people to behave in their
own best interest.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.150
It's in Fox's best interest for this show
to be a success, but they'd rather mess with

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:13.380
the show and have them fail, than allow creators
independence and let them succeed…They don't

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.700
like The Simpsons at Fox."

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.140
So how did this affect Futurama?

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.650
The network moved the show around from time
slot to time slot, then let it die a quiet

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.840
death in 2003 before it was eventually revived
by Comedy Central a few years later.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:32.040
But the network seemed to be working against
the show even before it debuted.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:37.280
When Futurama was originally coming down the
pike, Groening wanted Futurama to air at 8:30

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:42.150
PM on Sundays, directly after The Simpsons
and ahead of The X-Files in order to give

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.960
the show the best chance to find a large audience.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.980
This seemed like a no-brainer, but Fox disagreed,
for whatever reason, choosing instead to show

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:54.700
only two episodes of Futurama in the Sunday
night lineup before moving the series to a

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.860
much less desirable Tuesday night time slot.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.400
By the time the second season of Futurama
came around, Fox moved the show back to the

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.100
8:30 PM Sunday spot in which the first two
episodes aired.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:12.010
Then, in a move that alienated audiences further,
Fox shifted the show again in the middle of

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.700
the season, this time bumping it up to 7:00
PM on Sunday.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.780
And irregularly timed sporting events, which
were a huge money-maker for Fox, made it even

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.120
harder to anticipate when Futurama would air
each week.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.820
This up-and-down scheduling had another disappointing
consequence: Fox held onto episodes of Futurama

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:34.670
made for the third and fourth seasons and
reserved them for a fifth season…that didn't

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.680
even end up airing on the network.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:41.800
Fox never formally canceled Futurama, not
in the way that television series are usually

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:42.940
axed nowadays.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.370
The network simply stopped purchasing new
episodes of Futurama, and the series went

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:51.200
out of production ahead of the fall 2003 broadcast
season.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.200
"At least I still have my self respect!"

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.700
A couple years later, though, Comedy Central
picked up Futurama.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:06.170
The series lasted another three seasons on
the network before it ended in 2013, proving

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.080
Groening right and Fox wrong.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:13.040
In a 2003 interview with The Calgary Sun,
Groening offered his candid thoughts on the

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:13.540
situation:

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:18.120
"The people at Fox didn't ever support the
show and it wasn't to their taste and, in

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.020
my opinion, they're out of their minds.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.480
But they don't like The Simpsons either.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.180
The idea of a TV show that they haven't gotten
their greasy fingers all over creatively drives

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:27.860
them nuts.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:33.400
That's why almost everything else is so lousy…We
won the Emmy for best animated show and I

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.100
didn't even get a begrudging phone call from
anyone at Fox.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.300
That's a dark company that they can't even
make a fake phone call."

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.260
Ouch.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:42.960
Tell them how you really feel, Matt!

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.920
"Bite my colossal metal ass!"

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.820
Ultimately, though, Groening got the last
laugh.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:54.480
Futurama became a cult classic hit on a different
network, The Simpsons continues to run to

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.900
this day, and his show at Netflix, Disenchantment,
scored a second and third season in late 2018.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:04.160
You know what they say: living well is the
best revenge.

